{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor i in d['interpretations']:\n    if i['id']=='2318deef80994e8f8c04435040988c3d-interpretation-1':\n        print(json.dumps(i,indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"2318deef80994e8f8c04435040988c3d-interpretation-1\",\n \"investigation_id\": \"3f84facd1a81451882518e32ee8be535-question-0\",\n \"experiment_id\": null,\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"actor_drain\",\n  \"actor_pending\",\n  \"handle_contract\",\n  \"superseded_doc\",\n  \"test_ok_content\",\n  \"test_superseded_replace\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {},\n \"conclusion\": \"conditional\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n \"rationale\": \"The pending completion path can report a false success, under a schedule the actor does not exclude. A pending append_notify keeps only (assigned_idx, assignment_ballot). drain_notifiers evaluates, in order, Ok when assigned_idx <= decided, then Superseded when the assignment ballot is below the current promise ballot, then Timeout; the Ok arm reads no log entry and never checks that the value at assigned_idx is the caller's entry. The origin can hold an assignment made when it was leader or when a leader accepted its proposal, lose leadership to a higher ballot, and then have its own decided index advance past assigned_idx with a different value at that index: the runtime's own Superseded regression test constructs exactly that replacement (the old leader accepts locally with its outgoing cut, a new leader appends a fresh entry that decides at the same index, and the origin learns of the new ballot). Whether the pending resolves Ok or Superseded then depends only on whether a drain runs after the promise advanced but before decided reached assigned_idx. drain_notifiers runs only in the actor's tick branch; handling an incoming message never drains. Nothing orders a tick between the ballot change and the decided advance, so when the origin processes the higher-ballot Prepare and then the message that carries decided >= assigned_idx within one tick interval, the Ok arm wins and the caller is told its entry is decided at an index that holds a different entry. With a legal user-set tick_period that exceeds the leadership-turnover interval, that ordering is deterministic; with a short period it is a race. The gap on the reachable schedule is therefore answered on source grounds: no mechanism prevents it, and a legal configuration makes it the expected ordering.\",\n \"answers\": {\n  \"3f84facd1a81451882518e32ee8be535-gap-0\": {\n   \"explanation\": \"Reachable. drain_notifiers is invoked only from the tick branch (actor.rs tick handling), while handle_incoming_tracked processes messages without draining; the actor polls the tick first each iteration but the tick fires at most once per configured period. The ballot change (Prepare/AcceptSync from the new leader) and the decided advance (AcceptDecide/Decide from that leader) are separate messages that can both be processed inside one period. If the period exceeds the turnover interval, the pending sees decided >= assigned_idx and a stale assignment ballot at the same drain, and the Ok arm precedes the Superseded arm. Since tick_period is user-set and only advised to match the ServerConfig tick budget, this ordering is legal and deterministic in that configuration.\",\n   \"resolved\": true\n  }\n },\n \"knowledge\": [],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The Superseded regression test observes Superseded for the same replacement scenario, which shows the other ordering is common in its configuration; that is evidence about that schedule, not a mechanism that guarantees it.\",\n  \"When the new leader adopts the caller's value at assigned_idx, Ok is accurate and returning it must not be suppressed; the defect is limited to the replaced-value case.\",\n  \"The Superseded doc already calls the error a heuristic and tells callers to inspect the index, which mitigates the Superseded path but not a false Ok.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"No execution of the runtime crate is possible from the omnipaxos harness (omnipaxos_runtime is not a dev-dependency), so the schedule is established by source reasoning plus the runtime's own saved test expectations, not by a measured actor run.\",\n  \"The false Ok needs the caller's entry to have been accepted without a majority and then replaced at the same index; if the entry is adopted by the new leader, Ok is correct.\",\n  \"The exact duration of an in-process leadership turnover relative to a given tick_period is unmeasured here.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"2318deef80994e8f8c04435040988c3d\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
